traceability.evidence:
Implementation: - Deep validation rule implemented in src/rules/valid-req-reference.ts - JSDoc traceability: - @story docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md - @req REQ-DEEP-PARSE, REQ-DEEP-MATCH, REQ-DEEP-CACHE, REQ-DEEP-PATH - Core behavior: - loadAndCacheRequirements({ resolvedStoryPath, reqCache }): - Reads story file content with fs.readFileSync(resolvedStoryPath, 'utf8'). - Extracts requirement IDs using regex /REQ-[A-Z0-9-]+/g and adds them to a Set. - Caches the Set per resolvedStoryPath in reqCache (Map<string, Set>). - On read/parsing failure, catches the error and stores an empty Set, avoiding crashes (graceful error handling). - Satisfies REQ-DEEP-PARSE and REQ-DEEP-CACHE. - extractReqIdFromLine(line): - Splits an @req line on whitespace and returns parts[1] as the requirement ID. - Satisfies REQ-DEEP-PARSE for annotation lines. - validateAndResolveStoryPath({ comment, context, storyPath, cwd }): - Rejects storyPath containing '..' or path.isAbsolute(storyPath) and reports context.report({ messageId: 'invalidPath', data: { storyPath } }). - Resolves relative storyPath with path.resolve(cwd, storyPath) and ensures it stays within the project directory boundary. - Satisfies path-safety aspects (REQ-DEEP-PATH) and integrates with error reporting (invalidPath). - resolveStoryAndRequirements({ comment, context, storyPath, cwd, reqCache }): - Uses validateAndResolveStoryPath; on success, calls loadAndCacheRequirements to obtain reqSet. - Returns { resolvedStoryPath, reqSet } or nulls if path is invalid. - checkRequirementExists({ comment, context, reqId, storyPath, reqSet }): - If !reqSet.has(reqId), reports context.report({ messageId: 'reqMissing', data: { reqId, storyPath } }). - Enforces that @req references correspond to requirements present in the story file (REQ-DEEP-MATCH, REQ-DEEP-ERROR). - validateReqLine({ comment, context, line, storyPath, cwd, reqCache }): - Extracts reqId via extractReqIdFromLine. - Resolves story and requirements via resolveStoryAndRequirements. - Invokes checkRequirementExists when a valid reqSet is available. - Implements the full deep validation pipeline (parse, resolve, cache, match). - handleAnnotationLine / processCommentLines / handleComment / processAllComments: - Iterate over all JSDoc/raw comment lines, track current @story storyPath, and invoke validateReqLine for each @req. - Integrate deep validation with existing annotation-based flow (uses comments rather than AST nodes directly). - programListener(context) and exported create(context): - Initializes a shared reqCache and rawStoryPath per Program (per file). - Returns a Program visitor that calls processAllComments with the shared cache and cwd. - Ensures caching is scoped at the program level and integrates with ESLint's rule lifecycle. - meta.messages (user experience / error reporting): - reqMissing: "Requirement '{{reqId}}' not found in '{{storyPath}}'" - JSDoc references docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md and 007.0-DEV-ERROR-REPORTING.story.md with REQ-ERROR-SPECIFIC, REQ-ERROR-CONTEXT, REQ-ERROR-CONSISTENCY. - Provides clear, specific error messages including both the missing requirement ID and its story path. - invalidPath: "Invalid story path '{{storyPath}}'" - Also linked to 007.0-DEV-ERROR-REPORTING, maintaining consistent path-error messaging.
Integration with plugin: - src/index.ts - RULE_NAMES includes "valid-req-reference": - const RULE_NAMES = ["require-story-annotation", "require-req-annotation", "require-branch-annotation", "valid-annotation-format", "valid-story-reference", "valid-req-reference"] as const; - Dynamic loader: - RULE_NAMES.forEach((name) => { const mod = require(`./rules/${name}`); rules[name] = mod.default ?? mod; }); - Ensures the deep-validation rule is discoverable and loadable by ESLint. - TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES: - Maps "traceability/valid-req-reference" to "error", so missing/invalid @req references are treated as errors. - configs.recommended and configs.strict: - Built from createTraceabilityFlatConfig(), which includes the severity map above.
Tests for this story and rule: - tests/rules/valid-req-reference.test.ts - File-level annotations: - Tests for: docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md - @story docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md - @req REQ-DEEP-PARSE - Verify valid-req-reference rule enforces existing requirement content - Additional @story/@req for 007.0-DEV-ERROR-REPORTING to validate error messaging. - Uses RuleTester from eslint: - const ruleTester = new RuleTester({ languageOptions: { parserOptions: { ecmaVersion: 2020 } } } as any); - ruleTester.run("valid-req-reference", rule, { valid: [...], invalid: [...] }); - Valid cases: 1) "[REQ-DEEP-PARSE] valid requirement reference existing in story file": - code: "// @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
// @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE". - docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md defines **REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE** in its Requirements section. - Confirms matching works against real story requirements. 2) "[REQ-DEEP-BULLET] valid bullet list requirement existing in bullet story fixture": - code: "// @story tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md
// @req REQ-BULLET-LIST". - tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md: - "- REQ-BULLET-LIST - a requirement in bullet list format" - "- REQ-ANOTHER - another requirement". - Demonstrates that regex-based parsing correctly finds REQ- IDs in bullet-list format and non-story-doc paths (REQ-DEEP-FORMAT). - Invalid cases: 1) "[REQ-DEEP-MATCH] missing requirement in story file": - code: "// @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
// @req REQ-NON-EXISTENT". - Expects errors[0]: { messageId: 'reqMissing', data: { reqId: 'REQ-NON-EXISTENT', storyPath: 'docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md' } }. - Confirms missing requirements yield specific, contextual diagnostics. 2) "[REQ-DEEP-PARSE] disallow path traversal in story path": - code: "// @story ../docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
// @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE". - Expects messageId: 'invalidPath', data.storyPath: '../docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md'. - Validates path traversal handling and clear error messaging. 3) "[REQ-DEEP-PARSE] disallow absolute path in story path": - code: "// @story /absolute/path/docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
// @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE". - Expects messageId: 'invalidPath' with the absolute path. - Confirms absolute paths are rejected per security/validation requirements. 4) "[REQ-DEEP-BULLET] missing bullet list requirement in bullet story fixture": - code: "// @story tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md
// @req REQ-MISSING-BULLET". - Expects messageId: 'reqMissing', data.reqId: 'REQ-MISSING-BULLET', data.storyPath: 'tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md'. - Shows deep validation works with alternate formats/structures and produces correct errors when requirement is absent.
Story and fixture content: - docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md: - Contains requirement IDs used in implementation and tests: REQ-DEEP-PARSE, REQ-DEEP-MATCH, REQ-DEEP-FORMAT, REQ-DEEP-SECTION, REQ-DEEP-CACHE, REQ-DEEP-ERROR. - docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md: - Requirements section defines **REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE** and other REQ- IDs used in tests. - tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md: - Demonstrates bullet-list requirement formatting, which is successfully parsed by the regex-based deep validation.
Documentation: - docs/rules/valid-req-reference.md: - @story docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md - @req REQ-DEEP-PARSE, REQ-DEEP-MATCH, REQ-DEEP-PATH. - Describes behavior: - Verifies referenced story file exists and is project-relative. - Parses story file to extract REQ- IDs. - Ensures each @req matches a discovered requirement ID. - Reports "invalidPath" for unsafe/story paths and "reqMissing" when IDs are absent. - Includes correct and incorrect examples matching rule behavior and tests. - README.md: - Lists `traceability/valid-req-reference` as: "Validates that `@req` references point to existing requirement IDs" with link to docs/rules/valid-req-reference.md.
Tests execution: - package.json: - "test": "jest --ci --bail". - Running `npm test -- --verbose` via tooling yields: - > eslint-plugin-traceability@1.0.5 test - > jest --ci --bail --verbose - No failures reported in captured output, indicating the Jest test suite, including valid-req-reference tests, passes.
